1
00:00:01,030 --> 00:00:05,789
Over two thousand years ago, Rome kept
losing to Hannibal in open battle.

2
00:00:05,809 --> 00:00:10,896
So one general did something radical: he
refused the battles Hannibal wanted.

3
00:00:10,916 --> 00:00:12,736
His name was Fabius.

4
00:00:13,253 --> 00:00:15,431
Most trading bots want the battle.

5
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:20,934
They charge in, then show you a screenshot
of profit, taken after the market moved.

6
00:00:20,954 --> 00:00:23,724
You can’t check what they decided, or
when.

7
00:00:24,041 --> 00:00:29,321
Fabius is a paper-trading desk that
commits its decisions to BNB Chain before

8
00:00:29,341 --> 00:00:30,977
the outcome exists.

9
00:00:30,997 --> 00:00:33,157
Even the decision to do nothing.

10
00:00:33,609 --> 00:00:35,318
It starts with the rules.

11
00:00:35,338 --> 00:00:39,491
Each of our six bots has its strategy
hashed and locked on-chain.

12
00:00:39,511 --> 00:00:43,151
A strategy that wasn’t locked first can’t
commit a signal.

13
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:48,871
Every bar, a bot’s signals become one
Merkle root, committed to chain 97.

14
00:00:48,891 --> 00:00:53,304
Late commits are rejected. Every reveal is
checked against the root.

15
00:00:53,324 --> 00:00:56,674
Anyone can rerun the ledger. No keys
needed.

16
00:00:56,949 --> 00:00:58,969
On top runs the AI desk.

17
00:00:58,989 --> 00:01:05,449
Every five minutes, AI analysts, each with
an ERC-8004 identity, vote on which bot to

18
00:01:05,469 --> 00:01:06,853
run, and where.

19
00:01:06,873 --> 00:01:10,072
A locked formula turns their votes into
one book.

20
00:01:10,092 --> 00:01:14,192
And its root must reach the chain before
the five minutes are up.

21
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:18,120
The AI picks the rulebook. Code computes
the position.

22
00:01:18,391 --> 00:01:20,069
And the desk is open.

23
00:01:20,089 --> 00:01:24,475
Bring your own bot as declarative rules,
or plug in your own agent.

24
00:01:24,495 --> 00:01:29,875
Every bot runs the same gates in public,
and every verdict comes with its reason.

25
00:01:30,081 --> 00:01:34,175
Signals sell over x402, and the buyer pays
no gas.

26
00:01:34,195 --> 00:01:38,775
All on testnet, with a test token. No real
money, by design.

27
00:01:39,054 --> 00:01:41,964
Because here’s what we don’t claim:
profit.

28
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:44,875
The forward clock started on October 1st.

29
00:01:44,895 --> 00:01:50,645
To pass, a bot needs 20 signals, 20 days,
2 months, and a confidence interval above

30
00:01:50,665 --> 00:01:51,582
zero.

31
00:01:51,602 --> 00:01:54,122
Today, zero of six have passed.

32
00:01:54,361 --> 00:01:57,211
So Fabius does what Fabius does best.

33
00:01:57,691 --> 00:01:58,941
It waits.

34
00:02:00,207 --> 00:02:03,537
Fabius. Refuse the battle. Prove the
decision.
